// The board the "Belts that join" lesson starts on. A Source on a timer puts an item on its belt
// every 60 ticks, the pace a new Timer starts at. The belt runs four tiles east and stops short: its
// end docks to nothing, so items ride it, bunch at the end and fill it. A Sink sits three cells
// below the cell past the belt's end, turned once clockwise so its input faces north, up toward
// that cell. The lesson asks the user to draw on from the ring past the belt's end, straight down
// into the Sink's input, so the belt turns a corner on that cell and items reach the Sink. The run
// makes no outbound call.
//
//   row 2:   SOURCE 0 -b2------> (6,2) the empty cell past the belt's end
//   rows 3-5:                     (free)
//   row 6:                        SINK 1, input facing north
//
// The Examples list reads only the top of the boards folder, so this board never shows there.
//
// Handles mint in command order: the Source 0, the Sink 1, then the belt 2. The 6 commands and the
// history seal end the boot on tick 7.
//
// machine_kind u8 legend: SOURCE=0, SINK=7. Dock `port` is the catalog port index: SOURCE Out=0.
//
// Format 2 adds two fields a page reads and the core never does: `title`, the name a page shows,
// and `captions`, the ticks a viewer pauses on. This board has no captions.
Board(
    format: 2,
    title: "Belts that join",
    seed: 61,
    commands: [
        Place(kind: 0, cell_x: 1, cell_y: 2),        // 0: SOURCE
        Place(kind: 7, cell_x: 6, cell_y: 6),        // 1: SINK, Debug by default
        Rotate(node: 1, ccw: false),                 // the Sink's input turns from west to north
        DrawBelt(cells: [(2, 2), (3, 2), (4, 2), (5, 2)]),        // 2: its end at (5,2) docks to nothing
        Dock(belt: 2, endpoint: Tail, node: 0, port: 0),
        Configure(node: 0, config: Source(trigger: Timer(interval_ticks: 60))),
    ],
    script: [],
    captions: [],
    executor: Executor(default: Reply(after_ticks: 1), rules: []),
    view: View(fit: Board),
    end_tick: 360,
)
